# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RDDS — .gitignore
#
# The public repo carries the deployable system only: backend/, pipeline/,
# frontend/, db/, ml/detection/, README.md and the compose + requirements files.
# The research layer, the papers, the local docs and every heavy or regenerable
# artefact stay out (see "Local-only" at the bottom).
#
# Patterns that name a specific top-level directory of THIS repo are anchored
# with a leading slash, so a future frontend/src/data/ or backend/logs/ is not
# silently swallowed. Patterns meant to match anywhere are left unanchored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets — never commit environment files of any flavour.
# Deliberately redundant: *.env already covers .env, but this line is the one
# that must never be accidentally deleted.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Local tooling / IDE
/.venv
.idea/

# Python bytecode
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Node
/frontend/node_modules
/frontend/dist

# Model checkpoints, wherever they land.
# best.pt is 66 MB and GitHub hard-rejects anything over 100 MB. Weights are
# reproducible from the recorded seed + config, which is what ml/repro.py is for.
*.pt
*.pth
/ml/weights

# Heavy or regenerable output
/data
/logs
/runs
runs.zip
results.xlsx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only — present on disk, deliberately absent from the public repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Research layer (tooling, experiment artefacts and write-ups)
/ml/aws
/ml/research
/ml/depth
/ml/evaluation
/paper

# Internal documentation: the public repo keeps README.md alone
/CLAUDE.md
/TODO_CurrentSession.md
/docs/*.md
*.md
!README.md
.agents
.claude
skills-lock.json

# One-off setup, validation and dataset utilities
/scripts/*
landing-concepts
# Legacy directories, kept so they stay ignored if they reappear
/Documentation
/latex
